  "Question": "A collector offers to buy state quarters for \\(2000\\%\\) of their face value. At that rate how much will Bryden get for his four state quarters?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$20\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$50\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$200\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$500\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$2000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Four quarters have a total face value of \\(4\\times25=100\\) cents, or \\(\\$1\\). Since percent means per hundred,\n\\[\n2000\\%=\\frac{2000}{100}=20.\n\\]\nThe collector therefore pays \\(20\\times\\$1=\\$20\\), choice A.",
